# RME alignment with the internal memo of 2026-10-17 (rule 238)

Sprint record: `docs/sprints/dms-rme-comprehensive-closure-1.md` §2c (owner decisions 2026-11-17) and the memo
traceability record `docs/sprints/dms-rme-comprehensive-closure-1-memo-traceability.md`. The memo is held by the
owner; this public repository cites it by title and date only.

## 1. Payment totals need payment authority (memo M2.5, finding MEMO-F2)

The RME dashboard (`rme.dashboard`) is open to every holder of `view_clinic_visits`, clinicians included. Its two
payment cards, "Piutang RME Aktif" and "Pembayaran Hari Ini", are computed and rendered only for an account that holds
`manage_rme_billing` or `view_rme_payment_reports`, decided on effective permissions
(`RmeDashboardController::mayViewPaymentTotals()`, CG-06), never on a role name. For any other account the two
queries never run, so the figures cannot reach the view data. The clinical cards and the branch scope are unchanged.
Tests: `tests/Feature/RME/RmePaymentDashboardTotalsVisibilityTest.php` (PDV-01..06).

## 2. The planned treatment on the doctor's worklist (memo M3.2)

The treatment-room worklist (`rme.treatment-room-worklist.index`, the doctor's landing list) shows each visit's
"Tindakan Awal" (`initial_treatment_id`, required at registration), eager-loaded with the page
(`ClinicVisitRepository::worklistForBranches`), so the page runs one treatment query for any number of rows. The room
scope is unchanged. Tests: `tests/Feature/RME/DoctorRoomScopedWorklistTreatmentTest.php` (WT-01..04).

## 3. A Bank Transfer payment carries its reference (memo M5.1)

1. Every RME payment whose payment method has type `bank_transfer` (an instalment paid by transfer without a visit
   included) must carry a non-blank `reference_number`. The type is read from the stored `mst_payment_methods` row
   (`PaymentMethod::idRequiresTransferReference()`), never from anything the client sends about the method.
2. `CreateRmePaymentRequest` refuses a missing reference with `PaymentMethod::MESSAGE_TRANSFER_REFERENCE_REQUIRED`.
   `RmePaymentService::recordPayment()`, the only function that inserts an RME payment, re-asserts it, so the
   ordinary payment, the Kontrol allocation, the control-only payment and the visit allocation are all covered; the
   caller's transaction rolls back every row of the batch.
3. The payment form marks each method option with `data-requires-reference` and shows the field as required for a
   transfer (an Alpine hint; the server decides).
4. Other methods are unchanged. Lab billing (`app/Modules/Invoice`) is a separate domain (AIR-RMB-01) and outgoing
   refund settlements have their own method and proof rules (rules 213–216); neither is changed here.
5. `PaymentMethodFactory` defaults to `cash` (deterministic, CG-20); `bankTransfer()` gives a transfer method.

Tests: `tests/Feature/RME/RmePaymentTransferReferenceTest.php` (TR-01..07).

## 4. Not changed here (owner decision 2026-11-17: wait for the management payment discussion)

Additional lab fees, post-payment correction (PP-10), the correction roll-out beyond SPN4 and a backdating limit (D24)
stay REQUIRES OWNER DECISION. No supplementary invoice exists and an issued invoice stays immutable (rule 194).

## 5. CI

The three suites are selected by the existing `RmePayment` and `DoctorRoomScoped` critical-gate tokens in both runner
variants and declared in `config/ci_runner.php` `critical_gate_mandatory_suites` (CG-19).
